  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The successive 5 ionisation energies of an element are $800,2427,3658,25024$ and $32824 \\mathrm{~kJ} / \\mathrm{mol}$, respectively.\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{IE}_2}{\\mathrm{IE}_1}=\\frac{2427}{800}=3.03 \\\\\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{IE}}{\\mathrm{IE}_2}=\\frac{3658}{2427}=1.51 \\\\\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{IE}}{\\mathrm{IE}_3}=\\frac{25024}{3658}=6.84\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{IE}_5}{\\mathrm{IE}_4}=\\frac{32824}{25024}=1.31$\nSince ( $\\mathrm{IE}_4 / \\mathrm{IE}_3$ ) value is maximum, the element belongs to group 13.",
    "image": null
  },
